+## 24. Pass 13 — the day the brief changed the product set (2026-11-17, session `arena/58cbaaa2-zone1`)
+
+**Branch** `arena/58cbaaa2-zone1`, rebased onto `c6a143a` (the merge of PR #126, which had already
+landed the first product-intent register). **Evidence file:**
+[`reports/verification-2026-11-17-58cbaaa2.md`](reports/verification-2026-11-17-58cbaaa2.md).
+
+### 24.1 The finding that matters more than anything this pass built
+
+The brief supplied two more product links and a tracking ID. Re-resolved live, the two new links land
+on **a ThermoMaven instant-read thermometer and a CHEF iQ Sense Gen3 wireless thermometer** — filed by
+Amazon under *Thermometers & Timers › Meat*, not under *Fryers › Air Fryers*. So the submitted set now
+spans two categories while the site publishes one, and the commission analogy this project has used
+throughout (Kitchen 4.50%, S3) does not extend to them by inspection. Nothing was merged in: the links
+are recorded in the register, flagged as **F76**, and the decision about what the site is for is put in
+front of the owner as **SG-36 / Q-27**. An agent that "helpfully" wrote two thermometer pages from a
+fallback redirect would have spent the site's only durable asset — that every row can be checked — to
+gain two pages.
+
+### 24.2 The correction this pass owed the record
+
+Re-reading S6 (the only official page describing what a tracking ID is) surfaced two linked nodes, one
+of which refuted a reasoning step this project had been repeating:
+
+* **S39** states that *"it is not necessary for your unique ID to appear in order for us to track sales
+  made after the initial click through"*. The `tag=` parameter this site kept observing as *absent* from
+  landing URLs is therefore a **null** observation, not a negative one. Earlier passes had cited its
+  absence next to their cautions; that was an over-reading, and it is corrected on `links.html`, in
+  F78, Q-28, SG-37 and requirements row H-02 — dated and additive, with the historical rows left intact.
+* **S40** names the screen (`Manage your Tracking ID`), the **100 tracking IDs per account** limit and
+  the **Tracking ID Summary Report** where per-ID data is read — which is where the confirmation the
+  whole revenue path waits for actually lives. It is also the second official page carrying the screen
+  URL the register records, so that URL is quoted from Amazon rather than assumed.
+
+`shopnow047c-20` matches the shape S6 documents (`storeid-20`, sub-tags `storeid-1-20`). Shape is not
+existence, so the **special-link gate stays closed**: `check_special_link_gate()` fails the build if a
+tagged anchor appears while it reads closed, or if the gate is opened without a confirmation date and a
+cited source. No published link carries the tag; none is called invalid.
+
+### 24.3 What was built, in the order the brief asked for it
+
+| Layer | Deliverable |
+|---|---|
+| Intent register | `data/product-intent-confirmations.json` at schema v2 — `submitted_token` (exactly as supplied, 9 characters, against Amazon's 10-character ASIN definition, S23), `observation_2026_11_17`, `selected_tracking_id` with provenance / shape check / owner action / gate, and intended-vs-observed fields in **disjoint** objects. Rendered as `links.html`. |
+| Measurement | `data/measurement.json` → `measurement.html`: **5** events (outbound click, CTA impression, page arrival, guide reached end, first report row), each naming the decision it informs; `endpoint: null` recorded as a gap, not invented; an **8-column** campaign ledger with a filling rule per column and **0** rows; four anti-patterns ruled out (no clicks→sales conversion rate, no unsourced dashboard numbers, no "trending" label derived from on-site counts). |
+| Counter | Cookieless, request-free `localStorage` tally in the generated `assets/app.js` — per-page outbound counts, `IntersectionObserver` impressions at 0.55, a 40-key ceiling, export and erase — with the footer's Program Policies §3(e) statement rewritten to describe what it actually does, and every number labelled as one device's. |
+| Shopper polish | S-20 mobile-first pass: 44 px tap targets and a type floor on the mobile breakpoints, sticky comparison bar on `compare.html`. Presentation only; no published value moved. |
+| Decision layer | Suggestions **SG-36…SG-40** plus path **P6** ("Make the money path real"), questions **Q-27…Q-31**, topics **TP-21/TP-22** queued but not written, requirements **H-01…H-04**, programme flags **F76–F80**, sources **S36–S40** (40 registered, all official, all linked). |
+
+### 24.4 The defect class this repository keeps producing, caught again
+
+Ten passes typed "the three supplied links" into present-tense prose. The brief made every one of those
+sentences false on arrival, with each number inside them individually fine — the failure was in the
+*narrative*, not the data. Repaired where the tense is present: the footer, the landing-page status note,
+the category lede and the register page now take their counts from `len(records)` and
+`_links_in_category()`, four new tokens feed the requirements register, and `check_submitted_link_count()`
+fails the build on a mismatch. **Not** repaired, deliberately: the dated rows recording what an earlier
+pass observed while three links existed are statements about a past state, and the guard is scoped to
+present-tense surfaces so it cannot be satisfied by rewriting history. Process note: when the owner
+submits another link, add a record — never prose.
+
+### 24.5 What this pass refused to do
+
+No Amazon prices, star ratings, review counts or rankings (Policies §2(b)/§6(t); no PA-API/Creators
+credentials held). No photography at all, generated or copied — real imagery remains blocked on the
+owner's decision. No analytics endpoint, because static Pages hosting has nowhere to receive an event
+and a collector URL with nothing behind it is a promise. No ledger row, no conversion score, no revenue
+forecast. No unilateral edit to another session's published annex, and no claim that the supplied short
+links are invalid — their compliance status is unresolved (F78), and the site now says so in exactly
+those terms.
+
