+  "what": "Amazon's own tracking-ID mechanism already separates traffic sources without any script: extra tracking IDs on the same account each produce their own report, and the help page describes the pattern (storeid-20 with sub-IDs such as storeid-1-20). One ID per channel — site, newsletter, social — is measurement the site does not have to build, host or disclose a new technology for.",
+  "limit": "It attributes a channel, not a page. Clicks and orders arrive per tracking ID, not per URL, so a sub-tag plan answers 'which channel' and leaves 'which article' to EV-01/EV-03. S40 records a limit of 100 tracking IDs per associate account, so per-channel sub-tags are not a scarce resource at this site's scale.",
