l class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-08" value="B" data-sg="SG-08"><span>B. Add a cookieless, privacy-first analytics script</span><em class="tiny muted">effort M · risk medium</em></label><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-08" value="C" data-sg="SG-08"><span>C. Add full GA4 with goal events</span><em class="tiny muted">effort M · risk medium</em></label><label class="hold-row"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-08" value="HOLD" data-sg="SG-08"><span>Hold this one — change nothing</span></label><textarea class="dec-note" rows="2" data-sg="SG-08" placeholder="Optional: a condition, a date, or why. This travels with your choice."></textarea></fieldset><fieldset class="dec-row" data-sg="SG-14" data-title="Keep automated drafting, but make the claim-check gate the thing you trust" data-default=""><legend><a href="suggestions.html#sg-14">SG-14</a> Keep automated drafting, but make the claim-check gate the thing you trust <span class="pill pill-warn">waits for you</span></legend><p class="tiny muted">The brief asks for content generation at scale. That is achievable here - build.py already refuses to publish an article whose numbers do not appear verbatim in the verified dataset. The risk is the gate being treated as…</p><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-14" value="A" data-sg="SG-14"><span>A. Generate drafts from manufacturer documents only, and gate every number</span><em class="tiny muted">effort M · risk low</em></label><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-14" value="B" data-sg="SG-14"><span>B. Generate from the Amazon listings too</span><em class="tiny muted">effort M · risk high</em></label><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-14" value="C" data-sg="SG-14"><span>C. Write everything by hand</span><em class="tiny muted">effort L · risk low</em></label><label class="hold-row"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-14" value="HOLD" data-sg="SG-14"><span>Hold this one — change nothing</span></label><textarea class="dec-note" rows="2" data-sg="SG-14" placeholder="Optional: a condition, a date, or why. This travels with your choice."></textarea></fieldset><fieldset class="dec-row" data-sg="SG-17" data-title="Decide what happens to the eight superseded builds that are still published next to the live site" data-default="B"><legend><a href="suggestions.html#sg-17">SG-17</a> Decide what happens to the eight superseded builds that are still published next to the live site <span class="pill pill-ok">default B</span></legend><p class="tiny muted">The live site is not one site. This repository publishes 106 HTML pages, and only 27 of them are the maintained build generated by build.py. The rest are seven earlier or parallel builds (dashboard/, annex-88769516/, ses…</p><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-17" value="A" data-sg="SG-17"><span>A. Keep the parallel builds, but make the canonical build unambiguous</span><em class="tiny muted">effort S · risk medium</em></label><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-17" value="B" data-sg="SG-17"><span>B. Demote the superseded builds out of search without deleting them</span><em class="tiny muted">effort M · risk low</em><b class="tag-default">default</b></label><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-17" value="C" data-sg="SG-17"><span>C. Remove the duplicate pages and keep only their evidence files</span><em class="tiny muted">effort L · risk high</em></label><label class="hold-row"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-17" value="HOLD" data-sg="SG-17"><span>Hold this one — change nothing</span></label><textarea class="dec-note" rows="2" data-sg="SG-17" placeholder="Optional: a condition, a date, or why. This travels with your choice."></textarea></fieldset><fieldset class="dec-row" data-sg="SG-19" data-title="Give every published value a refresh date, and let the build report what has gone stale" data-default="A"><legend><a href="suggestions.html#sg-19">SG-19</a> Give every published value a refresh date, and let the build report what has gone stale <span class="pill pill-ok">default A</span></legend><p class="tiny muted">Every published figure on this site carries the date it was read, but nothing tells the owner when it should be read again. The dataset already contains a measured case of drift: Chefman&#x27;s own review counter moved f…</p><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-19" value="A" data-sg="SG-19"><span>A. Publish a stale-value report driven by the read dates the dataset already carries</span><em class="tiny muted">effort M · risk low</em><b class="tag-default">default</b></label><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-19" value="B" data-sg="SG-19"><span>B. Automate the re-fetch</span><em class="tiny muted">effort L · risk medium</em></label><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-19" value="C" data-sg="SG-19"><span>C. Freeze the values as a dated snapshot</span><em class="tiny muted">effort none · risk medium</em></label><label class="hold-row"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-19" value="HOLD" data-sg="SG-19"><span>Hold this one — change nothing</span></label><textarea class="dec-note" rows="2" data-sg="SG-19" placeholder="Optional: a condition, a date, or why. This travels with your choice."></textarea></fieldset><fieldset class="dec-row" data-sg="SG-21" data-title="Put the &quot;we could not confirm this&quot; markers on the money pages, not only on the register" data-default="B"><legend><a href="suggestions.html#sg-21">SG-21</a> Put the &quot;we could not confirm this&quot; markers on the money pages, not only on the register <span class="pill pill-ok">default B</span></legend><p class="tiny muted">The most distinctive thing this site does - refusing to guess, and publishing what it could not confirm - lives on a separate Flagged page that a reader has to go and find. On the buying guide that reads as thoroughness.…</p><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-21" value="A" data-sg="SG-21"><span>A. Put an inline marker next to each unconfirmed value on the product pages</span><em class="tiny muted">effort M · risk low</em></label><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-21" value="B" data-sg="SG-21"><span>B. Add a short trust strip under each buy button</span><em class="tiny muted">effort S · risk low</em><b class="tag-default">default</b></label><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-21" value="C" data-sg="SG-21"><span>C. Leave the register where it is</span><em class="tiny muted">effort none · risk low</em></label><label class="hold-row"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-21" value="HOLD" data-sg="SG-21"><span>Hold this one — change nothing</span></label><textarea class="dec-note" rows="2" data-sg="SG-21" placeholder="Optional: a condition, a date, or why. This travels with your choice."></textarea></fieldset><fieldset class="dec-row" data-sg="SG-22" data-title="Decide what the research agent is, and declare it in every request" data-default="A"><legend><a href="suggestions.html#sg-22">SG-22</a> Decide what the research agent is, and declare it in every request <span class="pill pill-ok">default A</span></legend><p class="tiny muted">The brief asks for an AI-powered platform that automates product research, and Amazon&#x27;s Program Policies contain a section written for exactly that case: IP License §4, the Agent Terms. Read live on 2026-11-16, they…</p><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-22" value="A" data-sg="SG-22"><span>A. Identify as an agent, and keep the research stage off Program Content</span><em class="tiny muted">effort S · risk low</em><b class="tag-default">default</b></label><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-22" value="B" data-sg="SG-22"><span>B. Ask Amazon first, then build</span><em class="tiny muted">effort S · risk low</em></label><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-22" value="C" data-sg="SG-22"><span>C. Leave the research stage manual</span><em class="tiny muted">effort none · risk low</em></label><label class="hold-row"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-22" value="HOLD" data-sg="SG-22"><span>Hold this one — change nothing</span></label><textarea class="dec-note" rows="2" data-sg="SG-22" placeholder="Optional: a condition, a date, or why. This travels with your choice."></textarea></fieldset><fieldset class="dec-row" data-sg="SG-25" data-title="One compliant call-to-action pattern on every money page — design it now, wire it when the tag exists" data-default=""><legend><a href="suggestions.html#sg-25">SG-25</a> One compliant call-to-action pattern on every money page — design it now, wire it when the tag exists <span class="pill pill-warn">waits for you</span></legend><p class="tiny muted">The site has exactly one call-to-action component and it lives on the three product pages only: a button reading &#x27;Open supplied Amazon link - verify model&#x27; with rel=&quot;nofollow sponsored&quot;. The compariso…</p><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-25" value="A" data-sg="SG-25"><span>A. Design the pattern now, publish it on the money pages, swap the destination later</span><em class="tiny muted">effort S · risk low — the disclosure and rel rules are already build-guarded</em></label><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-25" value="B" data-sg="SG-25"><span>B. Hold every CTA until the Associates tag is confirmed</span><em class="tiny muted">effort none · risk low</em></label><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-25" value="C" data-sg="SG-25"><span>C. Let each page improvise its own CTA</span><em class="tiny muted">effort S · risk medium — inconsistent disclosure placement</em></label><label class="hold-row"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-25" value="HOLD" data-sg="SG-25"><span>Hold this one — change nothing</span></label><textarea class="dec-note" rows="2" data-sg="SG-25" placeholder="Optional: a condition, a date, or why. This travels with your choice."></textarea></fieldset><fieldset class="dec-row" data-sg="SG-27" data-title="Review the shopper navigation labels now that a reader strip ships" data-default=""><legend><a href="suggestions.html#sg-27">SG-27</a> Review the shopper navigation labels now that a reader strip ships <span class="pill pill-warn">waits for you</span></legend><p class="tiny muted">The design-coherence pass (session 492acddc, PRs #111/#112) shipped a four-item shopper strip (Picks, Buying guide, Articles, Compare) in the topbar. The label set deserves a deliberate review now that the design system …</p><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-27" value="A" data-sg="SG-27"><span>A. Review the labels, then widen the strip if the review agrees</span><em class="tiny muted">effort S · risk low</em></label><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-27" value="B" data-sg="SG-27"><span>B. Leave navigation as the sidebar only</span><em class="tiny muted">effort — · risk none (status quo)</em></label><label class="hold-row"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-27" value="HOLD" data-sg="SG-27"><span>Hold this one — change nothing</span></label><textarea class="dec-note" rows="2" data-sg="SG-27" placeholder="Optional: a condition, a date, or why. This travels with your choice."></textarea></fieldset><fieldset class="dec-row" data-sg="SG-32" data-title="Add production-method authorship to every buyer-facing page - and a named editor when there is one" data-default=""><legend><a href="suggestions.html#sg-32">SG-32</a> Add production-method authorship to every buyer-facing page - and a named editor when there is one <span class="pill pill-warn">waits for you</span></legend><p class="tiny muted">The buyer-facing pages carry disclosure and sourcing but no byline and no visible &#x27;how this is made&#x27; statement on the page a shopper actually lands on. A reader deciding whether to trust a purchase recommendati…</p><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-32" value="A" data-sg="SG-32"><span>A. Name a human editor and publish an &#x27;About our standards&#x27; page</span><em class="tiny muted">effort M · risk none</em></label><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-32" value="B" data-sg="SG-32"><span>B. Ship a production-method byline line now</span><em class="tiny muted">effort S · risk none</em></label><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-32" value="C" data-sg="SG-32"><span>C. Status quo</span><em class="tiny muted">effort 0 · risk medium</em></label><label class="hold-row"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-32" value="HOLD" data-sg="SG-32"><span>Hold this one — change nothing</span></label><textarea class="dec-note" rows="2" data-sg="SG-32" placeholder="Optional: a condition, a date, or why. This travels with your choice."></textarea></fieldset><fieldset class="dec-row" data-sg="SG-12" data-title="Fix the flag register so a row number means one thing" data-default="A"><legend><a href="suggestions.html#sg-12">SG-12</a> Fix the flag register so a row number means one thing <span class="pill pill-ok">default A</span></legend><p class="tiny muted">Two different rows are both numbered F36. One says the short links&#x27; srctok marker is not constant; the other says a preset count was attributed to a source that does not state it. A register whose IDs collide cannot…</p><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-12" value="A" data-sg="SG-12"><span>A. Renumber the later row and add a build test that rejects duplicate IDs</span><em class="tiny muted">effort S · risk none</em><b class="tag-default">default</b></label><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-12" value="B" data-sg="SG-12"><span>B. Merge the two rows</span><em class="tiny muted">effort S · risk medium</em></label><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-12" value="C" data-sg="SG-12"><span>C. Leave it</span><em class="tiny muted">effort none · risk medium</em></label><label class="hold-row"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-12" value="HOLD" data-sg="SG-12"><span>Hold this one — change nothing</span></label><textarea class="dec-note" rows="2" data-sg="SG-12" placeholder="Optional: a condition, a date, or why. This travels with your choice."></textarea></fieldset><fieldset class="dec-row" data-sg="SG-13" data-title="Give the site a corrections log, and correct in public" data-default="A"><legend><a href="suggestions.html#sg-13">SG-13</a> Give the site a corrections log, and correct in public <span class="pill pill-ok">default A</span></legend><p class="tiny muted">This project&#x27;s most distinctive behaviour is refusing to guess and publishing what it cannot confirm. It has no mechanism for publishing a correction when a previously published value turns out to be wrong - the re-…</p><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-13" value="A" data-sg="SG-13"><span>A. Add a dated corrections table, fed from the re-verification data</span><em class="tiny muted">effort S · risk none</em><b class="tag-default">default</b></label><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-13" value="B" data-sg="SG-13"><span>B. Note corrections only in commit messages</span><em class="tiny muted">effort none · risk low</em></label><label class="hold-row"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-13" value="HOLD" data-sg="SG-13"><span>Hold this one — change nothing</span></label><textarea class="dec-note" rows="2" data-sg="SG-13" placeholder="Optional: a condition, a date, or why. This travels with your choice."></textarea></fieldset><fieldset class="dec-row" data-sg="SG-15" data-title="Add the two facts a buyer actually needs and the site does not have" data-default="A"><legend><a href="suggestions.html#sg-15">SG-15</a> Add the two facts a buyer actually needs and the site does not have <span class="pill pill-ok">default A</span></legend><p class="tiny muted">Across the three products the verified dataset is strong on capacity, temperature range and preset counts, and silent on the things that decide a purchase in a small kitchen: exterior dimensions and weight for the 6 Qt, …</p><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-15" value="A" data-sg="SG-15"><span>A. Add a &#x27;what the manufacturer does not publish&#x27; row to each product page</span><em class="tiny muted">effort S · risk none</em><b class="tag-default">default</b></label><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-15" value="B" data-sg="SG-15"><span>B. Ask the manufacturer for the missing figures</span><em class="tiny muted">effort M · risk low</em></label><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-15" value="C" data-sg="SG-15"><span>C. Buy and measure one unit</span><em class="tiny muted">effort L · risk medium</em></label><label class="hold-row"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-15" value="HOLD" data-sg="SG-15"><span>Hold this one — change nothing</span></label><textarea class="dec-note" rows="2" data-sg="SG-15" placeholder="Optional: a condition, a date, or why. This travels with your choice."></textarea></fieldset><fieldset class="dec-row" data-sg="SG-23" data-title="Settle product photography licensing before any image is published" data-default="C"><legend><a href="suggestions.html#sg-23">SG-23</a> Settle product photography licensing before any image is published <span class="pill pill-ok">default C</span></legend><p class="tiny muted">The design layer offers owner photos, licensed imagery and Amazon Program Content as image options, but no row records which images (if any) the site will publish, whose permission covers them, or how Program Content ima…</p><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-23" value="A" data-sg="SG-23"><span>A</span><em class="tiny muted">effort High · risk Low</em></label><label class="dec-opt"><input type="radio" name="dec-SG-23" value="B" data-sg="SG-23"><span>B</span><em class="tiny muted">effort Medium · risk Medium</em></label><labe