+<h2>Intended versus observed, kept apart</h2>
+<p class="small">Keep operator-confirmed product intent separate from observed Amazon redirect destinations. A redirect observation is not confirmation of the product the operator meant to promote.</p>
+<p class="small">Amazon&#x27;s own identifier definition states an ASIN is a 10-character number. Every one of the five submitted tokens is 9 characters, so each fails that definition on length alone. That does not make the links invalid or non-compliant — the short-link format, not the operator, chose the encoding, and no official Amazon page documents link.amazon (flag F16). It does mean the token cannot be used as a checkable product identifier, which is why the confirmation fields stay blank. <a class="src" href="https://kdp.amazon.com/en_US/help/topic/G200652190" title="Amazon.com Kindle Direct Publishing (help centre) — Linking from Your Website (KDP Help G200652190)" rel="noopener" target="_blank">S23</a></p>
