+<div class="reg-item" style="margin:.6rem 0 1rem">
+  <dl class="kv">
+    <dt>Provenance</dt><dd>Supplied in the project brief on 2026-11-17.</dd>
+    <dt>Shape check</dt><dd>Matches the published shape: a lower-case account-style prefix followed by the marketplace suffix, the same form as the help page&#x27;s own storeid-20 example. A shape match is not an existence check. <a class="src" href="https://affiliate-program.amazon.com/help/node/topic/GK5TZZ4AWML2QSLA" title="Amazon.com Associates Central — What are tracking IDs, and how does the new site help Associates use them?" rel="noopener" target="_blank">S6</a></dd>
+    <dt>What it cannot establish</dt><dd>Whether the ID exists on the account, whether it is the ID attached to any of the five submitted links, and whether the account is approved to earn. None of those is observable from outside Associates Central.</dd>
+    <dt>Your action</dt><dd>Open Associates Central → Manage your Tracking ID and confirm shopnow047c-20 is listed; then click through one published link and confirm the click appears in that ID&#x27;s report.
+      <a href="https://affiliate-program.amazon.com/home/account/tag/manage" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Associates Central → Manage your Tracking ID</a>
+      (about 5 minutes)</dd>
+    <dt>Enforced by</dt><dd>check_special_link_gate() in build.py — a tagged anchor while the gate is closed fails the build</dd>
