 <p class="small muted">A decision is only as good as the information behind it. This page separates four states that are usually mixed together: what we know and can prove, what we do not know but could look up, what the official source does not state, and what we cannot know at all without information that only the account holder possesses. Every suggestion on the Suggestions page points at the rows below that block it. Nothing here is a guess about what the answer probably is. Questions in the &#x27;known and sourced&#x27; state carry their answer on the row: an official source already settles them, and the answer is what the source says. Every other row states plainly that no answer is published, and names the step that would produce one.</p>
 
