+  <div class="twocol">
+    <div><p class="label">What we know, and can prove</p><ul class="tight"><li>Both links were re-read live on 2026-11-17: PI-04 lands on /dp/B0DHZTCNR5 and PI-05 on /dp/B0DZFD6R9Z, each carrying the same lv=shuf / plpRedirect=mhFallback fallback markers recorded for the original three links.</li><li>The served listing titles name a ThermoMaven instant-read thermometer and a CHEF iQ Sense Gen3 wireless thermometer; Amazon files both under Kitchen Utensils &amp; Gadgets &gt; Thermometers &amp; Timers &gt; Meat, not under Fryers &gt; Air Fryers.</li><li>The brands&#x27; own pages were read the same day: CHEF iQ states model CQ60-3C-Z3-E with five sensors and a 1,000 °F ambient rating for the iQ Sense; ThermoMaven&#x27;s site names its instant-read models F1 Pro and F1 Turbo and does not use the &#x27;1 Sec&#x27; label the observed listing carries.</li><li>The intended-product fields on both records are blank by design, and the observed destinations are stored in a separate field so the two can never be merged.</li></ul></div>
