+  <p><strong>Why it matters.</strong> Nothing on this site can earn until both halves are true. A tag that does not exist attributes nothing; a tag that exists but is not inside the link attributes nothing either. Everything else — content, design, measurement — is downstream of one screen in Associates Central.</p>
+  <div class="callout warn"><strong>Answer.</strong> No answer is published here. The official sources listed below were read and do not settle it, or it cannot be settled from outside the account. The "How to find it out" line names the step that would.</div>
+  <div class="twocol">
+    <div><p class="label">What we know, and can prove</p><ul class="tight"><li>The ID was supplied by the account holder on 2026-11-17 and recorded in the register as user-provided and unvalidated.</li><li>Its shape matches the only example Amazon publishes for a tracking ID — storeid-20, with sub-tag IDs of the form storeid-1-20 — read verbatim from the help node on 2026-11-17.</li><li>The help node states no validation rule and publishes no list of IDs per account, so a shape match cannot confirm existence.</li><li>The build now enforces the consequence: while the gate reads closed, every outbound link ships exactly as supplied and a tagged anchor fails the build.</li><li>Read the same day: Amazon&#x27;s help node states that a tracking ID does not need to appear in the click-through URL for the sale to be attributed, because the session is tagged on Amazon&#x27;s side (S39). The clean landing URLs recorded against these links therefore prove nothing either way, and an earlier pass&#x27;s reliance on that absence is corrected on the register page rather than edited out of history.</li></ul></div>
+    <div>
+      <p class="label">What is missing</p>
+      <p class="small">Two observations only the account holder can make: the ID listed at Associates Central &gt; Manage your Tracking ID, and a click-through appearing under that ID in the report.</p>
+      <p class="label">How to find it out</p>
+      <p class="small">Open Manage your Tracking ID (the screen S6 and S40 both name) and check for shopnow047c-20. Then click one published product link and confirm the click appears in that ID&#x27;s Tracking ID Summary Report — the URL you land on is not the evidence, per S39. Write the date into associates_central_confirmation_date, cite the screen as the source, and set tagging_gate.state to open.</p>
